From d52f4c8eb11406481756021dcea9bb10cdc29f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:42:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(properties): label the registration date RERA
 Received
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Quick Facts carried three date tiles that overlapped: Launch (the
registration date), Proposed Start (start of construction) and RERA
Completion. Under the agreed model the launch date IS the UP RERA
registration date, so Launch and a 'RERA Received' tile would show the
same value.

Two tiles now: RERA Received, holding the registration date, and RERA
Completion. Proposed Start is dropped from display — a straight rename of
that tile would have put 'RERA Received' above 15 Aug 2026 for ACE Arte,
which is when construction is proposed to begin, not when registration
came through on 28 Jul 2026. The value stays in rera_start_date, so
restoring the tile later is a one-line change.

The registration date also now renders through formatReraDate, so an ISO
value shows as '28 July 2026' rather than raw.
